WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.490
Episode 14

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.490
Ordeal in the Galaxy<i>!!
</i>First Launch of 2200<i>!!</i>

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.490
( Air date: Jan 05, 1975 )

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.700
Saraba Chikyuu yo

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.500
Tabidatsu fune wa...

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:40.650
...uchuu senkan Yamato

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.210
Space Battleship

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.210
<i>YAMATO</i>

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.100
Uchuu no kanata Iscandar he...

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.640
...unmei seoi...

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.510
...ima tobitatsu

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.510
Kanarazu koko he...

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.900
...kaette kuru to

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.320
Te wo furu hito ni...

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.700
...egao de kotae

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.710
Ginga wo hanare...

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.300
...Iscandar he...

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.500
...harubaru nozomu

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:17.200
Uchuu senkan Yamato

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.170
The primitive Octopus
Planetary Group...

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:38.930
...is one of the most dangerous
places in the Galactic System.

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:43.730
The eight solidifying
planets are still young...

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:49.500
{SONO}...and each produces a flow of water, and the
cores are bound by a belt of radiant energy.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:54.120
{SONO}And the flow strongly
interacts between the planets.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:59.790
{SONO}They're surrounded by a black cloud,
hiding everything within.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:06.980
{UCHUU}The space battleship Yamato has
been delayed for nearly three weeks.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.920
How about this ?

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.270
Check, Kodai.

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:43.700
Hey, w...wait, okay?

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:44.820
No.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.840
Hey, don't be so mean.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.520
I said, no.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.570
I don't want to change
what's been decided.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.200
You're so stubborn.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.170
I already
retracted many times.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:56.170
Say what ?

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.300
Why did you
do that, Kodai ?

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:00.770
Cool !

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:02.070
Go for it !

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.070
Hey, Kodai,
don't lose !

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.300
Shima, nail him !

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:04.970
Kodai, get him !

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.520
The scheduled
meeting will begin.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.260
All group leaders, report to
the planning room at once.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:12.790
You're a lucky bastard.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.090
You, too.
You owe me for this.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.760
Darn.  And it was just
getting interesting.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:17.260
It's over already ?

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.530
Central Planning Room

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:23.870
I think now is an appropriate time
to reevaluate our flight schedule.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.340
Shima, explain.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.320
Aye, sir.

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:36.250
Solar System

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:36.250
Galactic System

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:36.250
Planet Balan

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:36.250
Iscandar

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:36.250
Magellanic Cloud

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.770
Here is the flight path
prepared by the Yamato Project...

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:36.630
...of the Earth Defense Force just
before the launch of the Yamato.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:47.220
Solar System

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:40.810
{SHUPPATSU}We launched on
October 9th, 2199.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:43.990
{MAZU}First, we took ten days
to leave the Solar System.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.430
{SOKO}Then we took another ten days
to leave the Galactic System.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:52.870
{ZEN}We were supposed to reach the
mid-point, planet Balan, in 45 days.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:52.980
Planet Balan

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:59.940
Planet Balan

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:59.940
Iscandar

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:59.940
Magellanic Cloud

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:57.680
{BALAN}To get from planet Balan to the Large
Magellanic Cloud, where Iscandar is...

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.470
{BALAN}...another 45 days
is necessary.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:00.470
And...

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:07.910
Iscandar

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:07.910
Magellanic Cloud

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:06.920
{HOUSHANOU}...we assume that we'll stay on Iscandar to
obtain the radioactive purifier for 30 days.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:08.820
A total of 140 days.

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:13.770
{SORENI}On top of that, let's include 30 days
for combat and accidents...

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.270
...and 100 days for
the return trip.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.970
{NIHYAKU}We'll return to
Earth on the 270th day.

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:20.110
However, even if all
goes as planned...

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:24.820
...we'll only have 90 days until
the extinction of mankind.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:27.280
{TSUMARI}In other words,
it's a very tight schedule.

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:36.770
Solar System

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:36.770
Galactic System

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:36.770
Planet Balan

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:36.770
Iscandar

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:36.770
Magellanic Cloud

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:35.980
{SOSHITE}According to the plan, we should've
been nearing planet Balan today.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:41.920
{SHIKASHI}However, our current position is here,
just outside the Galactic System.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.730
Solar System

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.730
Galactic System

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.730
Planet Balan

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:42.950
Solar System

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:42.950
Galactic System

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:42.950
Planet Balan

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:42.950
Iscandar

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:42.950
Magellanic Cloud

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:45.870
{TSUMARI}So we're already
60 days behind schedule.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:51.120
{OMAKE}In addition, we've sat for 20 days in
front of the Octopus Planetary Group.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:58.660
You sound like we were delayed because
of too many battles with Gamilus.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.630
I didn't mean that.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:04.460
Then instead of wasting time
here, why don't we just go ?

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:07.620
You know we
can't do that yet.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.120
The reason why we've been
staying here for 3 weeks...

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:13.860
...is because we want to go to
Iscandar as soon as possible.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:14.870
{CHOTTO}Look at this.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:20.510
This is the Octopus Planetary
Group, and we are here.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:26.070
{KOKOKARA}There should be a strait, which leads to
the other side of the group, near here.

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:30.870
{KONO}There's a dark cloud surrounding
this planetary group...

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:35.100
...and since we don't know how
big it is, it's very dangerous.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:39.020
{OSORAKU}If we go around,
it might take 40 days.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:45.220
{SORE}If so, even if we have to wait for
20 days until this space storm is gone...

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.770
...it's quicker to go
through the strait.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:53.350
Do we even know when
the space storm will clear ?

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:55.320
Well, that's...

00:05:55.770 --> 00:06:00.140
Do we have to sit and wait for such an
uncertain opportunity, Chief Navigator ?

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:04.120
Besides, are you even sure
that the strait exists ?

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:05.240
It does.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.430
Have you seen it ?

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.370
No.
It's my intuition.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:10.430
Say what ?

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:13.870
Gimme a break !  The Yamato's
flight isn't like a chess game !

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.920
Even if you make a mistake,
you can't retract the move !

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:18.810
{NANIO}How could you...?  You're the
one who asked for a retraction !

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:31.280
In December 2199, the storm in the Octopus
Planetary Group hasn't weakened.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.090
Kodai, where are you going ?

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:49.540
I'm going to look for the
strait Shima was talking about.

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:55.120
Say what ?  If you go out in this
storm, you don't know what'll happen.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.230
You idiot.  It won't change the situation,
if you're concerned about that.

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:00.520
Kodai !

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.880
Chief Combat Commander !

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.520
Shut up.
Leave me alone.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:07.160
If there's no strait, we don't have
to sit and wait in a place like this.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:13.520
Kodai...

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:15.310
Once he's determined,
he never backs down.

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:28.410
Kodai, it's too dangerous
in this storm !

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:33.740
Launch.

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:43.950
No, the gauges
are useless !

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:51.100
Kodai !

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:01.660
Captain, I brought the
Chief Combat Commander.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:07.020
Kodai, why did you
act selfishly ?

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:10.480
Clean the hangar
as your punishment.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.670
Chief, thanks.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:17.240
Kato.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:18.060
Sir ?

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.310
You're no different.
You do it, too.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:25.800
It was your responsibility
to stop Kodai.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:30.410
Old geezer.

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:42.710
Move away, we're gonna
clean this place.

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:45.850
Wait a minute,
we're cleaning in here.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:48.120
Hey, don't you get it ?

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:51.160
We were punished by the Captain,
and we have to clean this place.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:52.800
We were punished, too.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.420
S...say what ?

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:57.950
Give me a break !
Everyone...?

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:02.190
I don't care if something
on the ship explodes.

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:03.620
This sucks.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:09.360
Rice cakes ?

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:14.230
If we leave things as they are,
we'll have another problem on the ship.

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:18.120
New Year's is soon and I want
to ease the tension on the ship.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.060
So I request
your permission.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:22.860
I can't.

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:24.460
You can't ?

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:27.980
Our food stock is
2 months, isn't it ?

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:29.420
Yes.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:34.920
We've been here for 3 weeks, and we
don't know when the storm will let up.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:39.500
{KARI}Even if we can get through, we don't know
when we'll find an alternate food supply.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:42.100
{TSUMARI}In other words, we
have too many uncertainties.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.450
I see.

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:48.820
The crew is stressed,
so don't tell them, okay ?

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:49.670
Aye, sir.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:28.760
Mr. Tokugawa...

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:30.710
Oh, Yabu.

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:33.040
What're you doing at
this time of night ?

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:38.420
We have nothing to do but to
sleep all day, so I'm not sleepy.

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:42.400
I wonder how much longer
we're going to be staying here.

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:48.070
If we delay this much, even if we
can obtain the Cosmo Cleaner D...

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:50.430
...we might not be able
to return in time.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:56.960
If so, maybe we should look for
a second Earth to migrate to.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:02.740
True.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:07.120
Hey Pops, if we can
reach outer space...

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.520
...there won't be very many
planets, unlike the Galactic System.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:11.990
It'll be impossible to find
a planet to migrate to.

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:15.120
That's true, but...

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:17.970
So, can you ask
the Captain about it ?

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:19.660
We can still turn around.

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:23.120
But...

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:34.850
Shima...

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:43.320
Shima, aren't you
going to sleep ?

00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:45.920
I can't sleep.

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:48.900
I wonder if the
strait really exists.

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:51.870
Why ?

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:55.470
You said it does.

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:59.200
That's true, but...

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:04.710
If you aren't confident, we should go
around the dark cloud as soon as possible.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:12.870
No, that's...

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:16.120
The strait should
be around here.

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:17.800
Sorry to bother you.

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:20.550
Good night.

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:54.590
Father, Mother...!

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:59.570
Father, Mother !

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:09.360
Mother...!

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:16.370
A dream ?

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:21.530
Oh, no.

00:13:26.590 --> 00:13:27.550
You're late, Kodai.

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:28.700
Sorry.

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:36.690
It's clear.
The storm is gone.

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:40.280
Hey Shima, look.

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:41.990
Look at the panel.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:46.860
A Gamilus ship ?

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:51.920
Stop thrusters, and go
beneath the flow of water.

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:53.480
Pay attention
to the radar.

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:55.810
Captain, let's shoot it down.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:59.160
Kodai, it's not a battleship.
Let it go.

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:00.610
Damn...

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.870
We shouldn't engage in
any unnecessary combat.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:16.950
Enemy ship is heading away.
Distance, 95,000 km.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.510
Where did it go ?

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:20.530
It must be
in the strait.

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:21.820
What ?

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:23.260
Kodai, go investigate.

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:25.460
A...aye, sir !

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:28.550
That's more like him.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:52.320
This is Kodai.
I found a strait-like opening.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:53.770
I'm entering now.

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:05.000
Oops.

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:20.040
Alright, this must
be the strait.

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:23.070
Yamato, Yamato...?

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:24.270
Damn, communications are down.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:35.780
I wonder what
happened to him.

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:40.320
Look, it's Kodai.

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:47.900
Yamato, Yamato, this is Kodai.
I found the strait.

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:12.140
I've returned
from reconnaissance.

00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:13.060
Good work.

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:16.140
Shima, I found it.
We can go through it.

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:17.630
So, how big is it ?

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:18.970
How big ?

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:20.520
Well...

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:25.310
Hey, didn't you make sure
we could go through it ?

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:29.460
Then we don't know if
it's the strait or not.

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:34.050
Captain.

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:35.770
Shima, it's alright.

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:39.520
It's good to be cautious, but we
can't wait for a 100% safety margin.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:41.200
We have to decide.

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:42.960
All hands, back
to your stations.

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:54.000
Mori.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:54.590
Sir ?

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:56.490
I'll permit you to
prepare the rice cakes.

00:16:56.930 --> 00:17:01.140
Once we're through the strait
it'll be New Year's, so get ready.

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:01.950
Aye, sir.

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:07.210
Hey, Shima.
Come with me.

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:09.870
What's the matter ?
I'm busy.

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:10.860
Just come with me.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:21.990
What's the matter, Kodai ?

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:27.520
My sloppy investigation might cause
the Yamato to be wrecked in the strait.

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:28.520
Isn't that right ?

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:35.070
I don't care what's gonna happen,
but before that, I want to do something.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:36.660
I'm gonna beat the
crap out of you.

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:43.020
Don't worry. "I" will guide the
Yamato through the strait safely.

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:46.460
But I have someone I want
throw out into the strait.

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.520
You know who,
don't you, Kodai ?

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:50.710
It's you !

00:17:58.300 --> 00:17:59.020
Damn you.

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.020
Stop !

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:17.290
What do you think you're
doing at a time like this ?

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:25.210
All ahead flank.
Port full.

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:28.870
All ahead flank.
Port full.

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:15.050
Damn, it's that storm again.

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:18.230
Auto-control won't be good enough.
Switching to manual.

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:22.380
Alright Shima, you have
complete control.

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:40.020
Extend the wings.

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:42.210
Aye, sir.
Extending the wings.

00:22:11.550 --> 00:22:12.070
We did it !

00:22:12.070 --> 00:22:13.120
We did it !

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:13.120
We did it !

00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:14.270
We did it, Shima !

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:16.070
It went great !
Hey, it went great !

00:22:16.070 --> 00:22:17.870
Thank goodness !

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:24.120
We made it !

00:22:24.120 --> 00:22:26.780
Good job, Kodai !
Good job !

00:22:27.100 --> 00:22:29.050
I envy men's friendships.

00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:52.520
Meanwhile, New Year's Day
has also come to Earth...

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:56.970
...but the radioactive poison continues
to penetrate ever deeper underground.

00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:17.920
The year 2200 has come.

